  <section class="v6-sec v6-w rv-in" aria-labelledby="hmlib"><div class="v6-hd"><h2 id="hmlib" class="v6-h">Start studying.</h2><a class="v6-a" href="/nclex-study-guides">Every guide ›</a></div>
   <div class="v6-rw"><div class="v6-row" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Study guides, swipe for more"><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/abg-interpretation" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#1d5670" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>ABG interpretation</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/abg-interpretation">ABG interpretation</a></h3><p>Read any blood gas in four steps, with compensation and the patterns the NCLEX likes to test.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/abg-interpretation">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/electrolyte-imbalances" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#7a3b52" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>Electrolyte imbalances</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/electrolyte-imbalances">Electrolyte imbalances</a></h3><p>Sodium, potassium, calcium and magnesium: what each imbalance looks like and what the nurse does first.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/electrolyte-imbalances">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/prioritization-and-delegation" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#3d5a3a" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>Prioritization and delegation</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/prioritization-and-delegation">Prioritization and delegation</a></h3><p>Who you see first, and who can safely do what: the rules behind the hardest questions on the exam.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/prioritization-and-delegation">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/lab-values-quick-reference" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#6b4a1f" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>Lab values quick reference</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/lab-values-quick-reference">Lab values quick reference</a></h3><p>Typical adult ranges for electrolytes, CBC, coagulation and ABGs on one printable page.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/lab-values-quick-reference">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#3b3f75" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>Heart failure: left vs right</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right">Heart failure: left vs right</a></h3><p>Left- vs right-sided signs, guideline medicines and daily weights.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/types-of-shock" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#24606a" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>Types of shock</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/types-of-shock">Types of shock</a></h3><p>The four types of shock: causes, signs and treatment side by side.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/types-of-shock">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/dka-vs-hhs" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#1d5670" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>DKA vs HHS</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/dka-vs-hhs">DKA vs HHS</a></h3><p>DKA vs HHS criteria and treatment order, including potassium before insulin.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/dka-vs-hhs">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article><article class="hm-card"><a href="/study-guides/high-alert-meds-and-antidotes" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="hm-cv" style="--cv:#7a3b52" aria-hidden="true"><span>Study guide</span><b>High-alert meds and antidotes</b><i>vexcura.com</i></div></a><h3><a href="/study-guides/high-alert-meds-and-antidotes">High-alert meds and antidotes</a></h3><p>High-alert medication classes and their antidotes and reversal agents.</p><a class="arw" href="/study-guides/high-alert-meds-and-antidotes">Read the guide<span aria-hidden="true"> &rarr;</span></a></article></div><div class="v6-arr" aria-hidden="true"><button type="button" class="v6-prev" tabindex="-1">‹</button><button type="button" class="v6-next" tabindex="-1">›</button></div></div>
